myapp/app.py<pre><code>from flask import Flask, g, jsonify
from sqlalchemy import select

from flask_tenants import FlaskTenants, tenant_required
from myapp.models import Patient
from myapp.tenancy import Session, manager


def create_app() -&gt; Flask:
    app = Flask(__name__)
    app.secret_key = "change-me"

    FlaskTenants(manager, app)

    @app.get("/healthz")
    def healthz():
        """No tenant needed — this must work before any tenant exists."""
        return jsonify(ok=True)

    @app.get("/patients")
    @tenant_required                      # (1)!
    def list_patients():
        with Session() as session:
            labels = session.execute(select(Patient.label)).scalars().all()
        return jsonify(tenant=str(g.tenant.tenant_key), patients=labels)

    return app
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Requests resolving to no tenant run in the shared schema by default, so a     health check and a signup page work. <code>@tenant_required</code> is how a route     opts into strictness.</li> </ol>
